{
  "name": "541. BFL key webhook_secret signs only trusted callback destinations (bfl webhook destination)",
  "description": "Pins TXE-7310: since TXE-7062 a bfl key's bfl_key_config.webhook_secret was sent to BFL beside any caller-supplied callback_url, so a caller could collect deliveries signed with the operator's secret and replay them to the operator's receiver. The key's secret now signs only a callback_url under one of bfl_key_config.webhook_url_prefixes (scheme, host and port, path at or below the prefix); any other callback_url is still sent as webhook_url, without the key's secret. Local fixture regression, no live provider calls: start tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs, start an isolated gateway on tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json and run with providerErrorFixture=1; every case is skipped otherwise. The fixture config's bfl key carries webhook_secret bfl-fixture-webhook-secret and webhook_url_prefixes [\"https://hooks.example.test/v/\"]. Rows 2 and 3: a callback_url on another host gets no key secret. Rows 4 and 5: a callback_url whose path climbs out of the prefix with .. gets no key secret. Rows 6 and 7: a callback_url under the prefix still gets the key's secret. Row 8: the management API returns the trusted prefixes as stored. Rows 9 to 12: the image edit task route (/v1/images/edits/tasks, its own conversion) applies the same rule, an untrusted callback_url gets no key secret and a trusted one does. Without the destination check rows 3, 5 and 10 fail. The URL matching rule is pinned by TestKeySecretMaySignFor in core/providers/utils, the provider by TestBFLKeyWebhookSecret in core/providers/bfl, and the class by TestKeySigningSecretsHaveADestinationAllowlist in core/schemas.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "541.1 reset the fixture's counters (bfl webhook destination)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{providerErrorFixtureUrl}}/__reset",
          "host": [
            "{{providerErrorFixtureUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "__reset"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('the fixture reset its counters', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
